  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The analysis is entirely theoretical and does not provide empirical case studies or quantitative risk assessments of specific urban AI deployments.",
      "what": "This conceptual study analyzes the security and accountability deficits of urban AI systems integrated into public infrastructure and services. It frames these systems as complex socio-technical networks that currently operate without the standardized risk measures and national oversight frameworks applied to commercial AI.",
      "why": "It establishes a theoretical foundation for regulating municipal algorithms, shifting the focus from purely technical security to the broader socio-technical vulnerabilities of daily public services."
    }
  },
